    "descriptionModule": {
      "briefSummary": "The CRASH-19 trial is a multinational, open-label, factorial, randomised trial in adults hospitalised with suspected or confirmed acute COVID-19 infection.",
      "detailedDescription": "We will evaluate the effect of aspirin (150mg once daily), losartan (100mg once daily), and simvastatin (80mg once daily) in patients with COVID-19 infection.\n\nEligible patients will be randomly allocated to one of eight study arms (aspirin only; losartan only; simvastatin only; aspirin and losartan; aspirin and simvastatin; losartan and simvastatin; aspirin, losartan and simvastatin; standard care only). Trial treatments are given in addition to the usual standard of care at the study hospital.\n\nTreatment will be started as soon as possible after randomisation and will continue until death, discharge or 28 days after randomisation, whichever occurs first."
    },
